2-Methoxy-6-(2-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl)naphthalene (Table 5, entry 4).
Following the general procedure using 1-bromo-2-(trifluoromethyl)benzene
(113 mg, 0.50 mmol) and (6-methoxynaphthalen-2-yl)boronic acid (152 mg,
0.75 mmol) the reaction was allowed to stir for 4 h. After column
chromatography, the product wasobtained as a white solid (152 mg, 99%).
Mp 68-70 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.81-7.75 (m, 3H), 7.73 (s, 1H),
7.62-7.56 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 1H), 7.53-7.49 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 1H), 7.46-7.40
