$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for Suzuki-Miyaura Couplings (Table 5). Arylboronic
acid (0.75-1.00 mmol) and Pd(dtbpf)Cl2 (6.5 mg, 0.01 mmol) were added
under an Ar atmosphere in a 5.0 mL microwave vial with magnetic stir bar
and Teflon-lined septum. Aryl bromide (0.50 mmol), triethylamine (0.21
mL, 1.50 mmol), and surfactant solution (1.0 mL, 2 wt % in degassed
water) were sequentially added into the reaction under a flow of Ar. The
reaction was allowed to stir vigorously for 2-11 h. The reaction mixture
was then diluted with EtOAc, passed through a silica gel bed, and further
washed with EtOAc to collect the coupling product. All volatile solvent
was removed in vacuo to obtain crude product that was further purified by
flash chromatography on silica gel. [1,1' -Biphenyl]-3-carbonitrile
(Table 5, entry 1). Following the general procedure using
3-bromobenzonitrile (91 mg, 0.50 mmol) and phenylboronic acid (91 mg,
0.75 mmol) the reaction was allowed to stir for 2 h. After column
chromatography, the product was obtained as a colorless liquid (61 mg,
99%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.89-7.86 (t, J = 1.5 Hz, 1H), 7.85-7.80
(dt, J = 7.8, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 7.66-7.62 (dt, J = 7.8, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 7.60-7.54
(dt, J = 8.0, 1.5 Hz, 3H), 7.52-7.46 (tt, J = 7.3, 1.5 Hz, 2H), 7.46-7.40
(tt, J = 7.3, 1.5 Hz, 1H).30
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, yield depends on reaction conditions (reagent)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM "Nok": A Phytosterol-Based Amphiphile Enabling Transition-Metal-Catalyzed
Couplings in Water at Room Temperature
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Klumphu, Piyatida; Lipshutz, Bruce H.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2014), 79(3), 888-900

