$DATUM Butyl
4-(7-(10-(bis(4-hexylphenyl)amino)-1-(2-hexyldecyl)-1H-phenanthro[1,10,9,8-cdefg]carbazol-3-yl)benzo[c][1,2,5]thiadiazol-4-yl)benzoate
(7). In a three-neck round bottom flask, 5 (220 mg, 0.22 mmol), 6 (88 mg,
0.22 mmol), Pd(PPh3)4 (4 mg, 0.004 mmol), and Na2CO3 (230 mg, 2.20 mmol)
were dissolved in a solvent mixture of ethanol/benzene/H2O (14 mL, v/v/v,
1/4/2). The reaction mixture was stirred at reflux under argon for 12 h.
Water was added and the mixture was extracted three times with
chloroform. The organic phase was washed with water and then dried over
anhydrous sodium sulfate. After solvent removal under reduced pressure,
the residue was purified by column chromatography (toluene/petroleum
ether 60 -90 °C, v/v, 1/1) on silica gel. A red oil as the desired
product (204 mg, 91% yield). 1H NMR (400 MHz, THF-d 8) δ: 8.72-8.69 (m,
2H), 8.29-8.24 (m, 4H), 8.20 (s, 1H), 8.10 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 8.04 (br,
2H), 7.97 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H), 7.87 (s, 1H), 7.69 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H),
7.66 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 7.15 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 4H), 7.06 (d, J = 8.2 Hz,
4H), 4.58 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 2H), 4.40 (t, J = 6.4 Hz, 2H), 2.60-2.57 (m,
4H), 1.86-1.79 (m, 2H), 1.66-1.63 (m, 4H), 1.60-1.54 (m, 2H), 1.38 (br,
18H), 1.19 (br, 18H), 1.07-1.04 (m, 4H), 0.96-0.93 (m, 6H), 0.87-0.80 (m,
6H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, THF-d 8) δ: 166.53, 156.82, 154.84, 14 8.10,
143.31, 142.79, 136.74, 136.10, 134.34, 133.37, 132.97, 132.79, 131.96,
131.66, 131.26, 130.52, 130.21, 129.90, 129.45, 129.23, 128.87, 126.68,
125.82, 125.71, 125.63, 125.13, 124.23, 122.74, 122.25, 121.93, 118.74,
117.22, 116.62, 65.43, 50.64, 41.0 7, 36.34, 32.97, 32.89, 32.76, 32.03,
31.03, 30.72, 30.61, 30.38, 30.18, 27.51, 23.66, 20.37, 14.67, 14.65,
14.37. MS (ESI) m/z calcd. for (C77H90N4O2S): 1134.68. Found: 1135.69
([M+H]+). Anal. calcd. for C77H90N4O2S: C, 81.44; H, 7.99; N, 4.93.
Found: C, 81.43; H, 7.92; N, 4.96.
