$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Suzuki-Miyaura Cross-Couplings (A). In an
oven-dried Schlenk tube backfilled with argon, a mixture of nucleoside 2
(1.0 equiv), boronic acid or ester (1.5 equiv), AcOK (1.5 equiv),
Pd(dppf)Cl2 (0.05 equiv), was heated at 90˚C in dioxane (0.08M) for 18h.
The reaction was cooled to room temperature and diluted with CH2Cl2. The
solution was filtered through a pad of Celite and extensively washed with
CH2Cl2. The filtrate was concentrated under reduced pressure and the
residual oil was purified by column chromatography on silica gel to
provide biaryl nucleosides 6a-h.
1’-(3’-O-tertbutyldimethylsilyl-5’-O-triisopropylsilyl-2’-deoxy-β-D-ribofuranoside)-6-phenylquinazoline-2,4-(3H)-dione
(6a). According to the general procedure A, the biaryl nucleoside 6a was
obtained after column chromatography on silica gel (hexane/EtOAc, 90:10 →
85:15) using nucleoside 2 (0.400 g, 0.637 mmol), phenylboronic acid
(0.117 g, 0.956 mmol), AcOK (0.094 g, 0.956 mmol) and Pd(dppf)Cl2 (0.026
g, 0.032 mmol). White foam, (0.361 g, 91%). Rf(hexane/EtOAc, 8:2): 0.31;
[α]D26 +30.3 (c 0.5, CHCl3); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 9.56 (s, 1H),
8.46 (s, 1H), 7.85 (s, 2H), 7.62 (d, J1 = 7.6 Hz, 2H), 7.47 (t, J1 = 7.6
Hz, 2H), 7.40-7.36 (m,1H), 6.82 (t, J1 = 7.6 Hz, 1H, H1’), 4.78 (quint,
J1 = 4.0 Hz, 1H, H3’), 4.08 (dd, J1 = 11.2 Hz, J2 = 2.8 Hz, 1H, H5’),
3.96(dd, J1 = 11.2 Hz, J2 = 3.2 Hz, 1H, H5’), 3.90-3.87 (m, 1H, H4’),
2.88-2.81 (m, 1H, H2’), 2.10 (ddd, J1 = 13.2 Hz, J2 = 7.6Hz, J3 = 3.6 Hz,
1H, H2’), 1.19-1.09 (m, 21H), 0.92 (s, 9H), 0.12 (s, 3H), 0.11 (s, 3H);
13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ:162.2, 150.2, 139.1, 139.0, 136.7, 133.4,
129.2, 128.0, 126.9, 126.7, 117.7, 117.3, 86.6, 84.2, 70.4, 62.1, 37.2,
26.0, 18.2, 12.2, -4.4, -4.6; IR (neat) ν: 3192, 3067, 2944, 2864, 1688,
1620, 1471, 1367, 1320, 1251, 1109, 1065,1050, 881, 834, 777, 759, 731,
676 cm-1; HR-ESI MS (m/z): [M + Na]+ calcd for C34H52N2O5Si2Na 647.33125,
found 647.33145.
