$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1. General procedure for the Suzuki-Miyaura
coupling of boronate 6 with bromoindoles: An oven-dried 10 mL Schlenk
flask was charged with boronate 6, bromoindole (1 equiv), Pd2(dba)3 (1
mol%), XPhos (4 mol%) and K3PO4.H2O (3 equiv) The flask was evacuated and
refilled with argon three times. Dioxane (10 mL) and degassed water
(100μL) were added and the flask was equipped with a reflux condenser.
The reaction mixture was heated at reflux over night. Purification on
silica gel column chromatography afforded the desired coupling product.
Preparation of methyl
3-(2-(methoxycarbonyl)-1-benzyl-5,6-dimethoxy-1H-indole-4-yl)-1-benzyl-5,6-dimethoxy-1H-indole-2-carboxylate
9: The general procedure was used with bromide 2b (45 mg, 0.11 mmol),
boronic ester 6 (50 mg, 0.11 mmol), K3PO4.H2O (77 mg, 0.33 mmol),
Pd2(dba)3 (1 mg, 0.0011 mmol) and XPhos (2 mg, 0.0044 mmol). Purification
on silica gel column chromatography (20-30% EtOAc/hexane then 0-10%
EtOAc/methylene chloride, Rf = 0.22 in 20% EtOAc/hexane) afforded 9 as a
white solid (63 mg, 85%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, acetone-d6, ppm): δ 7.32-7.14
(m, 12H), 6.88 (d, 1H, 0.7 Hz), 6.72 (s, 1H), 5.99-5.88 (m, 4H), 3.92 (s,
3H), 3.85 (s, 3H), 3.72 (s, 3H), 3.64 (s, 3H), 3.46 (s, 3H), 3.39 (s,
3H); 13C {1H} NMR (100 MHz, acetone-d6, ppm): δ 163.3, 162.7, 154.4,
151.6, 147.6, 144.4, 139.9, 137.3, 134.8, 129.3, 127.9, 127.4, 127.2,
126.5, 125.2, 122.8, 121.1, 120.5, 119.1, 112.0, 103.4, 94.4, 93.9, 60.7,
56.4, 56.3, 56.2, 51.6, 51.4, 48.6, 48.3; IR (cm-1, CH2Cl2 film): 2950,
1704; Anal. Calcd for C38H36N2O8: C, 70.36; H, 5.59; N, 4.32, found: C,
70.44; H, 5.84; N, 4.16; LC-HRMS: Calcd for C38H36N2O8 ([M+Na]+)
671.23639, obsd 671.23749; m.p. 173.8-174.5 °C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki-Miyaura cross-coupling reaction
