$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1. General procedure for the Suzuki-Miyaura coupling of boronate 6 with
bromoindoles: An oven-dried 10 mL Schlenk flask was charged with boronate
6, bromoindole (1 equiv), Pd2(dba)3 (1 mol%), XPhos (4 mol%) and
K3PO4.H2O (3 equiv) The flask was evacuated and refilled with argon three
times. Dioxane (10 mL) and degassed water (100μL) were added and the
flask was equipped with a reflux condenser. The reaction mixture was
heated at reflux over night. Purification on silica gel column
chromatography afforded the desired coupling product. Preparation of
methyl
3-(2-(methoxycarbonyl)-1-benzyl-5,6-dimethoxy-1H-indol-3-yl)-1-benzyl-5,6-dimethoxy-1H-indole-2-carboxylate
8: The general procedure was used with bromide 1b (45 mg, 0.11 mmol),
boronic ester 6 (50 mg, 0.11 mmol), K3PO4.H2O (76 mg, 0.33 mmol),
Pd2(dba)3 (1 mg, 0.0011 mmol) and XPhos (2 mg, 0.0044 mmol). Purification
on silica gel column chromatography (40%-50% EtOAc/hexane, Rf = 0.29 in
40% EtOAc/hexane) afforded 8 as a white solid (43 mg, 60%). 1H NMR (400
MHz, acetone-d6, ppm): δ 7.32-7.28 (m, 4H), 7.23-7.21 (m, 2H), 7.16-7.13
(m, 6H), 6.73 (s, 2H), 6.07 (d, 2H, 16Hz), 5.85 (d, 2H, 16Hz), 3.85 (s,
6H), 3.64 (s, 6H), 3.42 (s, 6H); 13C {1H} NMR (100 MHz, acetone-d6, ppm):
δ 163.4, 151.5, 147.5, 140.1, 134.8, 129.3, 127.8, 127.2, 124.6, 120.7,
118.3, 103.3, 94.4, 56.3, 56.2, 51.3, 48.6; IR (cm-1, CH2Cl2 film): 2988,
2949, 1697; Anal. Calcd for C38H36N2O8: C, 70.36; H, 5.59; N, 4.32,
found: C, 70.41; H, 5.67; N, 4.25; LC-HRMS: Calcd for C38H36N2O8
([M+Na]+) 671.23639, obsd 671.23496; m.p. 205.8-206.2 °C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimized on bases and solvents, optimization study, Suzuki-Miyaura
cross-coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
